Pokémon originated from Satoshi Tajiri's childhood hobby of catching insects near Tokyo. He partnered with Ken Sugimori and others at Game Freak to create the concept, originally called "Capsule Monsters" (inspired by the Game Boy Link Cable and Ultraman series). Nintendo funded 6 years of development after Shigeru Miyamoto pitched it. The first games, Pocket Monsters Red and Green, launched in Japan on February 27, 1996 for Game Boy. The name changed to Pokémon due to trademark issues. The franchise became a worldwide phenomenon through games, anime (1997), trading cards, and merchandise. It's now estimated as the world's highest-grossing media franchise, spanning nearly three decades with over 1,000 Pokémon species created.